# rule 11: where we_fileop.c resolves a path.  The walk of a folder resolves
# none: every entry is a folder's descriptor and a name.  These are the
# paths the user typed (opened once, at the boundary) and the wastebasket,
# a folder of ours the owner names itself, 0700 and checked before use.
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_parent_open|1|keep|the folder of a path the user typed, opened once
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_job_open_src_path|1|keep|a single file's typed source, through its one opener
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_job_open_dst_path|1|keep|a single file's typed destination, through its one opener
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_root_source_open|1|keep|the typed source folder, through its one opener
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_root_dst_parent|1|keep|the typed destination folder, through its one opener
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_remove|1|keep|a single file's typed path, through its one opener
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_tree_inside|3|keep|the real paths of the two typed names, read only
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_tree_link_text|1|keep|the real path of the typed source, read only, for the text of the links
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_job_place|1|keep|drops the second name of a replaced file in the wastebasket
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_wastebasket_open|1|keep|opens the wastebasket without following a link
we_fileop.c|r11:fileop_remove_into_wastebasket|2|keep|the typed path into the wastebasket's free name
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_wastebasket|3|keep|makes and checks the wastebasket (mkdir, open, access)
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_wastebasket_slot|1|keep|looks for a free name in the wastebasket
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_in_wastebasket|3|keep|the real paths of the wastebasket and the typed name, read only
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_mkdir|1|keep|the File Manager's dialog, on a name the user typed; a later pass may move it onto (parent, name)
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_rmdir|1|keep|the File Manager's dialog, on a name the user typed
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_chmod|2|keep|the File Manager's dialog, on a name the user typed
we_fileop.c|r11:wpe_fileop_rename_noreplace|2|keep|a folder's rename the File Manager asks for by two typed names

